{% doc %}
  Renders the search field and everything that hangs off it.

  The input is a real `<input type="search" name="q">` inside a
  `<form action="/search">`, so pressing Enter with JavaScript disabled runs a
  normal search. Everything else is enhancement.

  The ARIA wiring is the combobox pattern: the input owns `role="combobox"`,
  `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, and `<search-list>` reports the active
  option through `aria-activedescendant` on the input. Focus never leaves the
  field — moving it into the suggestions closes the mobile keyboard.

  ## Two variants, one snippet

    overlay  The drawer and the modal. A head row with the field, a column of
             recent searches and suggested tags, and a results column that shows
             merchant-picked suggestions until the customer types.
    inline   A field with a dropdown beneath it. Used on the 404 page, where
             there is no panel to fill and no room for a sidebar.

  The idle column is not decoration. An empty search panel asks the customer to
  guess what the store sells; recent searches, tags and a few chosen products
  give them something to click before they have typed a character.

  @param {string} [id] - Input id. Default SearchInput
  @param {string} [variant] - 'overlay' | 'inline'. Default 'inline'
  @param {string} [layout] - 'modal' | 'drawer'. Overlay only, drives the head row
  @param {boolean} [close] - Render the overlay close button in the head row

  @example
    {% render 'predictive-search', id: 'SearchDrawerInput', variant: 'overlay',
       layout: settings.predictive_search_layout, close: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign input_id = id | default: 'SearchInput'
  assign panel_id = input_id | append: 'Results'
  assign resolved_variant = variant | default: 'inline'
  assign resolved_layout = layout | default: 'modal'
  assign is_overlay = false
  if resolved_variant == 'overlay'
    assign is_overlay = true
  endif

  comment
    Three placeholder fields in Theme settings, rotated one at a time. A single
    static placeholder in a supplement store says nothing; rotating prompts
    show three things the customer could actually ask for. The first is what
    renders server-side, so there is never an empty field before the script
    loads, and it is the only one a customer with JavaScript off ever sees.
  endcomment
  assign prompt_1 = settings.search_input_placeholder
  if prompt_1 == blank
    assign prompt_1 = 'search.placeholder' | t
  endif

  assign prompts = prompt_1
  if settings.search_input_placeholder_2 != blank
    assign prompts = prompts | append: '|' | append: settings.search_input_placeholder_2
  endif
  if settings.search_input_placeholder_3 != blank
    assign prompts = prompts | append: '|' | append: settings.search_input_placeholder_3
  endif

  assign suggested_tags = settings.search_suggested_tags | default: '' | split: ','

  comment
    Count on a product_list setting, with size as the fallback. The two are
    interchangeable on this drop depending on the platform version, and a nil
    count compared against zero fails silently — the merchant picks six
    products, the panel shows none, and there is nothing to debug.
  endcomment
  assign suggestion_products = settings.suggestion_product_list
  assign suggestion_count = suggestion_products.count | default: suggestion_products.size | default: 0

  assign suggestion_collections = settings.suggestion_collection_list
  assign suggestion_collection_count = suggestion_collections.count | default: suggestion_collections.size | default: 0

  comment
    Articles come from a blog picker rather than an article picker, because
    Shopify has no article_list setting. Taking the newest few from the chosen
    blog is also the behaviour a merchant actually wants: the panel stays
    current on its own instead of pointing at three posts from last spring
    until someone remembers to change them.
  endcomment
  assign articles_limit = settings.suggestion_articles_count | default: 3
  assign suggestion_blog = blogs[settings.suggestion_blog]
  assign suggestion_articles = suggestion_blog.articles

  assign show_suggestion_products = true
  if settings.show_suggestion_products == false
    assign show_suggestion_products = false
  endif

  assign show_suggestion_collections = true
  if settings.show_suggestion_collections == false
    assign show_suggestion_collections = false
  endif

  assign show_suggestion_articles = true
  if settings.show_suggestion_articles == false
    assign show_suggestion_articles = false
  endif

  comment
    Whether anything at all sits in the idle column. The Browse all link is
    rendered from this rather than from the product group alone — a panel
    showing only collections still needs its way out.
  endcomment
  assign has_suggestions = false
  comment
    The products group counts even with nothing chosen, because it falls back to
    placeholder rows — and a column with rows in it still needs its way out.
  endcomment
  if show_suggestion_products
    assign has_suggestions = true
  endif
  if show_suggestion_collections and suggestion_collection_count > 0
    assign has_suggestions = true
  endif
  if show_suggestion_articles and suggestion_articles.size > 0
    assign has_suggestions = true
  endif
-%}

<predictive-search
  class="predictive-search predictive-search--{{ resolved_variant }}"
  data-section-id="predictive-search"
  {% if is_overlay %}data-layout="{{ resolved_layout }}"{% endif %}
  data-prompts="{{ prompts | escape }}"
  data-recent-limit="{{ settings.recent_searches_limit | default: 6 }}"
  {% if settings.show_recent_searches == false %}data-recent-disabled{% endif %}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The head row exists only in the overlay. Inline — the 404 page — the field
    is the whole component, and a heading and a close button above it would be
    furniture for a panel that is not there.

    The drawer shows the title; the modal hides it in CSS rather than dropping
    it from the markup, so the dialog keeps its accessible name in both layouts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if is_overlay -%}
    <div class="search-panel__head">
      <h2 class="search-panel__title">{{ 'search.title' | t }}</h2>
  {%- endif -%}

    <form class="search-form" action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search">
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="{{ input_id }}">{{ 'search.label' | t }}</label>

      <input
        id="{{ input_id }}"
        data-ref="input"
        class="search-form__input"
        type="search"
        name="q"
        value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
        placeholder="{{ prompt_1 | escape }}"
        role="combobox"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="{{ panel_id }}"
        aria-autocomplete="list"
        aria-haspopup="listbox"
        autocomplete="off"
        spellcheck="false"
        enterkeyhint="search"
      >

      {%- comment -%}
        The animated prompt. Empty in the markup and filled by JavaScript, which
        also clears the input's own `placeholder` at the same moment — so a
        customer without JavaScript keeps the plain placeholder above and never
        sees an empty field, and there is no frame where both are painted.

        `aria-hidden` because the field already has a real `<label>`, and
        `pointer-events: none` in CSS so a click on the words lands in the input.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="search-form__prompt" data-ref="prompt" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">

      {%- comment -%}
        No `hidden` attribute: `display: none` cannot transition, and this button
        appears and disappears between keystrokes. CSS hides it with
        `visibility` instead — still out of the accessibility tree, still out of
        the tab order via `tabindex`, but able to fade.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="search-form__reset"
        data-ref="reset"
        aria-label="{{ 'search.clear' | t }}"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        {% render 'icon', icon: 'close', size: 16 %}
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        The spinner lives inside the submit control and sits on top of the
        magnifier rather than beside it. Both are absolutely centred in the same
        circle, so the swap is two opacity changes and nothing in the field
        moves — a loader that takes its own space would push the field's
        contents sideways on every keystroke.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="submit" class="search-form__submit" aria-label="{{ 'search.submit' | t }}">
        {% render 'icon', icon: 'search', size: 18 %}
        <span class="search-form__spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="visually-hidden" data-ref="busy"></span>
      </button>
    </form>

    {%- if close -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign search_close_label = 'accessibility.close_search' | t
      -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Secondary rather than primary. The green submit control sits a few
        pixels away inside the field; two green circles side by side, one of
        which cancels and one of which searches, is a coin toss.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'button',
         label: search_close_label,
         id: 'SearchClose',
         class: 'close-search-drawer',
         icon: 'close',
         variant: 'secondary',
         size: 'small',
         icon_only: true,
         attributes: 'data-overlay-close' %}
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- if is_overlay -%}
    </div>

    <div class="search-panel__body" data-lenis-prevent>
      <div class="search-panel__aside">
        {%- comment -%}
          Recent searches are per-browser, so the list is written by JavaScript.
          The section around it ships hidden and is revealed once there is
          something in it — an empty "Recent searches" heading is worse than no
          heading at all.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <section class="search-block search-recent" data-ref="recent" hidden>
          <div class="search-block__head">
            <h3 class="search-block__title">
              {{- settings.recent_searches_text | default: 'Recent searches' | escape -}}
            </h3>

            <button type="button" class="search-recent__clear" data-ref="recentClear">
              {% render 'icon', icon: 'trash', size: 14 %}
              <span>{{ 'search.clear_recent' | t }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <ul class="search-chips" data-ref="recentList" role="list"></ul>
        </section>

        {%- if suggested_tags.size > 0 -%}
          <section class="search-block search-tags">
            <h3 class="search-block__title">
              {{- settings.suggested_tags_text | default: 'Suggested tag' | escape -}}
            </h3>

            <ul class="search-chips" role="list">
              {%- for tag in suggested_tags -%}
                {%- assign tag_label = tag | strip -%}
                {%- if tag_label == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                <li>
                  <button type="button" class="search-chip" data-search-term="{{ tag_label | escape }}">
                    {{- tag_label -}}
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="search-panel__main">
        <div class="predictive-search__panel" id="{{ panel_id }}" data-ref="panel" hidden>
          {%- comment -%}
            Filled by sections/predictive-search.liquid. Empty on first render so
            nothing flashes before the customer has typed anything.
          {%- endcomment -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The idle column. Hidden by CSS the moment the panel opens, rather than
          removed, so returning to an empty field brings it straight back with
          no second request.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="search-panel__idle" data-ref="idle">
          {%- comment -%}
            Three merchant-curated groups, each independently switchable, each
            rendered through the same card as a real suggestion — so what the
            customer sees before typing is shaped exactly like what they see
            after, and the panel does not appear to change layout mid-search.

            `selectable: false` throughout: these rows sit outside the combobox
            popup, and `role="option"` on a list item that no listbox owns is
            invalid ARIA rather than a harmless extra attribute.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if show_suggestion_products -%}
            <section class="search-suggestions">
              <p class="search-group__title">
                {{- settings.suggestion_text | default: 'Suggestion products' | escape -}}
              </p>

              {%- if suggestion_count > 0 -%}
                <ul class="search-group__items" role="list">
                  {%- for product in suggestion_products limit: 6 -%}
                    {% render 'predictive-search-card',
                       type: 'product',
                       item: product,
                       id: 'SearchSuggestionProduct-',
                       index: forloop.index,
                       selectable: false %}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Nothing chosen yet. A heading over an empty column reads as a
                  panel that failed to load, so the shape of the list is shown
                  with example rows instead — clearly marked as examples, and
                  not links.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {% render 'predictive-search-placeholder', count: 3 %}
              {%- endif -%}
            </section>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_suggestion_collections and suggestion_collection_count > 0 -%}
            <section class="search-suggestions">
              <p class="search-group__title">
                {{- settings.suggestion_collections_text | default: 'Popular collections' | escape -}}
              </p>

              <ul class="search-group__items" role="list">
                {%- for collection in suggestion_collections limit: 6 -%}
                  {% render 'predictive-search-card',
                     type: 'collection',
                     item: collection,
                     id: 'SearchSuggestionCollection-',
                     index: forloop.index,
                     selectable: false %}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </section>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_suggestion_articles and suggestion_articles.size > 0 -%}
            <section class="search-suggestions">
              <p class="search-group__title">
                {{- settings.suggestion_articles_text | default: 'From the journal' | escape -}}
              </p>

              <ul class="search-group__items" role="list">
                {%- for article in suggestion_articles limit: articles_limit -%}
                  {% render 'predictive-search-card',
                     type: 'article',
                     item: article,
                     id: 'SearchSuggestionArticle-',
                     index: forloop.index,
                     selectable: false %}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </section>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if has_suggestions -%}
            <div class="search-results__footer">
              <a class="search-results__all" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">
                <span>{{ settings.browse_all_text | default: 'Browse All' | escape }}</span>
                {% render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-right', size: 16 %}
              </a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="predictive-search__panel" id="{{ panel_id }}" data-ref="panel" data-lenis-prevent hidden></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p class="visually-hidden" data-ref="status" role="status"></p>
</predictive-search>
